WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.420
<i>Summer break of my 
second year in middle school.</i>

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.740
<i>I'd just had my first-ever date
 at a summer festival days prior,</i>

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.940
<i>and I hadn't been able 
to stop myself sighing since.</i>

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.820
I love Irido-kun.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.130
Irido Mizuto

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.130
Remind Me

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.130
Message

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.130
Decline

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.130
Accept

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.620
H-Hello?

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.070
<i>Hey. Is... now a good time?</i>

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.790
Y-Yup! Absolutely!

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.640
I wasn't doing much anyway!

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.720
S-So, what's up?

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.080
D-Did you need something?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.790
<i>No, not really.</i>

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.360
Oh, okay.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:52.910
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.490
<i>I just felt like talking to you.</i>

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.930
Huh?!

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.660
U-Um... Me too.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.460
I've been wanting to talk to you too.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.840
<i>Really? Perfect timing, then.</i>

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.340
Y-Yeah, it is!

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.320
It must be pretty windy out, huh?

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.260
<i>Oh... Yeah.</i>

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:24.800
<i>Ayai?</i>

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.820
Hmm?

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:26.680
<i>Never mind.</i>

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.530
<i>Actually, my battery's getting pretty low.</i>

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.140
Oh, I understand.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.030
Can we talk some other time, Irido-kun?

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.840
<i>Yeah, of course.</i>

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.830
<i>I'm sure I'll see you in the library 
the day after tomorrow.</i>

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.740
Okay. I can't wait.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.010
<i>Talk to you then.</i>

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:45.740
Yeah.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:47.540
<i>Bye.</i>

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.970
Bye-bye.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.250
<i>Why couldn't we talk
while his phone was charging?</i>

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.360
<b>My Stepmom's 
Daughter Is 
My Ex</b>

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:38.440
<b>The Former Couple Visits Relatives</b>

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:38.440
<b>"I Guess You Could Say She Loved to Laugh"</b>

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.080
Welcome! It's nice to meet you.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.950
I'm Irido Natsume.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.090
N-Nice to meet you too!

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.930
I'm Irido Yuni.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.200
Sorry for not introducing myself sooner.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.670
No, no! The same goes for me.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.630
Now then, you must be Yume-chan.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.580
Yes, I'm Irido Yume.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.630
Thank you for having us.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.150
My, my! How polite!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.140
What a nice young lady you are.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.090
I trust you're getting along with Mizuto.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.690
Y-Yes...

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.280
They're practically closer 
than we are, in fact.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.190
It's true! Mizuto's been such a gentleman.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.320
Right, Yume?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:23.440
Hey, Mizuto-kun! It's been too long!

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.720
Long time no see, Madoka-san.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.660
What a relief. I see you're 
still a man of few words.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.580
I wasn't sure what I'd do if you'd decided
to reinvent yourself as a high schooler.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:38.290
High school isn't the time
 to go reinventing yourself.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.570
Wow, harsh.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.300
Yuni-san, Yume-chan, 
allow me to introduce you.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.990
These are my uncle's grandchildren.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:50.100
I guess that'd make them your 
second cousins, Yume-chan.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.810
Meet Tanesato Madoka-chan 
and Tanesato Chikuma-kun.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.340
I see what's going on here.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.200
Um, is something the matter?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:07.950
Not a thing.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.700
Yup, yup...

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.720
In just a little bit,

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.580
the whole family's going to be having 
a welcome barbecue down by the river.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.430
In our swimsuits, of course!

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.950
Are you both enjoying the food?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:53.980
Yes, we are.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.500
It's delicious.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.670
I gotta say, you did a 
fine job raising Mizuto-kun.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.640
You really came through, Mineaki-kun.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.660
It's really something.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.690
Thank you very much.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:13.930
Uncle Mineaki became a single father not 
long after Mizuto-kun was born.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:18.140
Apparently, Granny Natsume 
helped out from time to time,

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.010
but it couldn't have been easy.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.710
The whole family was worried 
about him, you know?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.820
Which is why... How should I put it?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:34.330
We want to welcome you and Yuni-san 
with open arms, you could say.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.830
I'm grateful.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.220
<i>It's clearer to me now than ever.</i>

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.200
<i>Mineaki-san remarrying was a testament</i>

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.550
<i>to overcoming a great hardship in his life.</i>

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.990
<i>Because of that, I have to...</i>

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:57.080
<i>We have to protect this new 
family of ours no matter what.</i>

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.180
By the way, Yume-chan...

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.330
You're so skinny! How is your waist so thin?!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.440
I-I'm just not very muscular, that's all.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.720
I'm so freaking jealous!

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.150
And that bikini's gorgeous!

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.540
Did you pick it out yourself?

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.620
Um... Well, kinda.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:16.970
Your boyfriend?

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.160
No, it's not like that.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.780
I see, I see. Not there yet, huh?

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.290
Well... not exactly....

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:26.340
Huh?

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.800
Wh-Wh-What?!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.360
Do you mean what I think you mean?!

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.710
N-No way! Absolutely not!

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.920
That reaction makes it
 even more suspicious!

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.250
I'm telling you the truth.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.440
I feel a little left out, though.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.770
He never seemed to want to open up to me.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.850
Really? I had no idea.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.530
It's true!

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.650
I've been watching over 
him since kindergarten,

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.910
but I get the cold shoulder 
whenever I try to talk to him.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.180
Does that mean...

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:01.620
Dad.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.880
I'm done eating, so I'm heading back.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.630
Sure. Thanks, kid.

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:09.440
<i>Thanks? For what?</i>

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:10.560
Later.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.220
Huh?!

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.040
You're kidding! You're leaving already?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.140
We haven't gotten in the water yet!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.010
I'll pass!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:21.160
Unbelievable! How can you come 
to the river and not even swim?

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.390
At the very least, I'm not letting 
Yume-chan get away!

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:26.020
What?

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.400
Off with you!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.600
M-Madoka-san, sto—

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:30.620
All right!

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.020
Time to settle our tummies 
with a little swimming!

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:49.800
Oh, Yume-chan.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.810
Go get some rest once 
you're done with those, okay?

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:54.140
Are you sure?

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.460
This lot isn't going to bed any time soon.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.470
Duly noted.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:02.220
Oh, could you let Mizuto-kun know 
it's his turn in the bath?

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.770
He's probably in Great-Grandpa's study.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.460
Oh, it's you. What's up?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.790
It's your turn to take a bath.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.550
That time already?

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:38.930
The Siberian Dancing Girl

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.420
You're not going to use a bookmark?

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:43.980
No need. I remember the whole story anyway.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:44.650
Huh?

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:47.190
You won't find this book anywhere else, see.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:55.650
The Siberian Dancing Girl

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.690
I reread it every time we come back here.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:53.510
"The Siberian Dancing Girl"?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.240
It's my great-granddad's autobiography.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.960
Wow, his autobiography?

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:58.780
Wait...

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.910
He published it himself.

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:05.410
Well, it was never sold or distributed, 
so I guess it's just a hand-bound book.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.910
Pretty weird hobby, huh?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:12.710
I'd just started elementary school when 
I first stumbled upon it in this study.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:17.290
There's no author listed, so it struck
 me as mysterious, you know?

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:19.680
I couldn't help but open it.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.680
The Siberian Dancing Girl

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.340
I've read it every year since.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.710
Is it really that interesting?

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.120
It was full of words I didn't know,

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.690
so it was largely impenetrable
 to me at the time.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:33.210
And yet, for whatever reason, 
I read it through to the end.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:38.740
The Siberian Dancing Girl

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.010
It was the first story that I 
ever read all by myself.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.310
The first story you read by yourself...

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.540
The Siberian Internment.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:48.790
After the war, he was held captive in 
the Soviet Union for three or four years.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.480
This book is about his time there.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.910
So who's the "dancing girl"?

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.140
Remember Mori Ogai?

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.300
Elise?

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.260
Exactly. He wrote about a 
woman he met in Siberia,

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.910
just like Mori Ogai did in "The Dancing Girl."

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:07.430
Well, if you want to know the rest, 
why not read it for yourself?

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.680
Huh?

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.940
Books are meant to be read, no?

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.770
If you're so inclined, how about it?

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.390
It's short, so it shouldn't take you long.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.120
Are you sure?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.070
You act like something bad's going to happen.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.390
I'm gonna go take a bath now.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:24.320
Hey.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:25.530
Hmm?

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.560
Has anyone else ever read this?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:30.150
I mean... I really doubt it.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:34.210
It was pretty tucked away 
when I first found it.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.210
<i>Not Mineaki-san, Natsume-san,</i>

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:45.220
<b>The Siberian Dancing Girl</b>

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.760
<i>and not even Madoka-san have ever read this.</i>

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.620
<i>The book that shaped Irido Mizuto...</i>

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.600
<i>Does he really not mind sharing it with me?</i>

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.470
Oh no, what have I done?

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.720
I should dab that off...

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:49.500
Alone in this study secluded 
from the outside world,

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:55.190
as if to separate himself from its reach...

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:01.350
He's been sequestered in
this room his entire life.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.630
Make it to the end?

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:07.880
Yeah.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:09.700
I see.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:14.390
Your great-granddad was in love back then.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.480
Say, do you mind... if I ask 
what your first love was like?

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:23.990
Huh?

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:31.490
I guess you could say she loved to laugh.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:36.920
I see.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:39.840
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:43.460
<i>His first love had to be...</i>

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:46.360
<i>Madoka-san after all.</i>

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.970
<b>My Stepmom's Daughter Is My Ex</b>

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:55.690
We've got plenty to choose from, 
so pick whichever suits your fancy!

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.600
Thanks, Granny!

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:01.430
What kind of yukata would you like, Yume-chan?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.860
Hmm...

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.220
You're thin, and your hair's nice and long,

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.320
so I bet you'd look good 
in any traditional clothes.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.890
I can't wait for the summer festival!

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:14.520
The weather's supposed to be good,
so the fireworks should be quite a sight.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:16.960
Yume-chan?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.840
Did something happen between 
you and Mizuto-kun?

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:27.840
It's not about anything that he did.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:33.380
I'm just in my own head 
about how selfish I've been.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.310
<i>That's it. I finally understand.</i>

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:41.500
<i>He's his own living, breathing person.</i>

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:45.940
<i>He isn't some perfect manifestation 
of my dreams or ideals.</i>

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.720
<i>He ostracized himself from others,</i>

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.890
<i>living in complete isolation before we met.</i>

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.100
<i>It's not crazy to think a boy like him</i>

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:59.100
<i>would've fallen for someone else before me.</i>

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:05.050
Are you in love with Mizuto-kun?

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:11.200
I don't know...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:15.260
How do you define loving someone?

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:18.840
It's simple, isn't it?

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.730
Your heart races when you're near them.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.260
And you find yourself daydreaming 
about kissing them.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:25.820
If that's your experience, 
the diagnosis is clear, no?

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:29.360
But how is that any different from lust?

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.350
Whoa there, now someone's 
asking the tough questions.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.320
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.390
Listen...

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.580
Aren't you constantly invalidating 
your own emotions, Yume-chan?

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:39.530
Huh?

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:45.020
You're always looking for excuses to 
justify <i>not</i> being with Mizuto-kun, right?

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:48.620
<i>I'm looking for excuses not to be with him?</i>

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.840
Now, now! Don't look so puzzled.

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:55.180
There's no need to think so hard on it.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:16:00.360
Just take the opportunity to
 start sorting out those feelings.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.710
Y-You say that, but I have 
no idea where to start.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.940
No worries! Your cousin's got an idea!

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:22.590
<i>I wonder what exactly she's planning.</i>

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.780
Sorry! Something came up and I just 
can't get out of it, you know?

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:28.880
It's not a problem.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.380
Thanks a ton!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:37.210
There should be a light bulb somewhere 
in that chest of drawers over there,

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:39.040
so have a look for it 
with Yume-chan, will you?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.640
I'll leave you all alone
 for about half an hour, 'kay?

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:47.400
Absolutely no one, not even Aunt Yuni and
 Uncle Mineaki, will be by, you hear?

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.390
<i>Th-That was dreadful.</i>

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.900
<i>I didn't realize Madoka-san 
was such an atrocious liar.</i>

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:55.780
What's up?

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:59.160
You have something you want 
to tell me, don't you?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.950
Why else would you have her arrange this?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.100
<i>I have no idea what to say first.</i>

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.820
<i>I scarcely know what my problem is,</i>

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.100
<i>let alone how to go about solving it.</i>

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:24.330
<i>After coming here</i>

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.540
<i>and getting to know my new relatives,</i>

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.650
<i>I feel like I'm finally part of the family.</i>

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.400
<i>Then in that old study,</i>

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.400
The Siberian Dancing Girl

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.400
<i>I discovered the book that 
shaped the boy I know today.</i>

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:38.150
<i>And in doing so,</i>

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:41.380
<i>it made me realize how selfish I've been.</i>

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:47.320
<i>Getting the wrong idea and wasting 
his time just like I am now...</i>

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:53.130
<i>Getting mad at him, getting snarky, 
and treating him unfairly...</i>

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:59.300
<i>I'm lugging around feelings 
I should have let go of long ago.</i>

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:03.560
<i>I get it now. I think I finally understand.</i>

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:08.330
<i>I know what's wrong with me,
 how to fix it...</i>

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.020
<i>and what I need to tell him right now.</i>

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.480
<i>It's not gonna make it all better.</i>

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.160
<i>It's going to feel like ripping off the scab</i>

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:21.900
<i>that's formed over my broken heart.</i>

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.840
<i>I'm sure it'll be painful.</i>

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:26.360
<i>Excruciating.</i>

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:29.020
<i>But even so, if I...</i>

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.420
<i>If we're ever going to move on,</i>

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:33.710
<i>I need to face this</i>

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:37.850
<i>and finally accept the heartbreak
 of my first relationship.</i>

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:40.840
Irido-kun...

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.760
Irido-kun... Irido-kun...

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:55.130
<i>Irido-kun, you were my first love.</i>

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:56.940
<i>And yet...</i>

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.890
<i>When you said you wanted to break up,</i>

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:04.440
<i>it felt like a weight was 
lifted off my shoulders.</i>

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:08.380
<i>"It's finally over. I'm finally free."</i>

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:14.070
<i>"I no longer have to feel 
hurt, sad, or alone anymore."</i>

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:16.840
<i>That's how I truly felt deep down.</i>

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:19.090
<i>But still...</i>

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.640
<i>I never wanted us to break up.</i>

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.840
<i>I should have called you that summer.</i>

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.690
<i>And I should have bought you 
something for Christmas.</i>

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:39.720
<i>I should have made you 
chocolate for Valentine's.</i>

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:43.580
<i>And I should have told you I didn't want to</i>

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:46.060
<i>when you said we should break up.</i>

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:53.420
<i>There's just so much I
regret not doing, Irido-kun.</i>

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.280
Irido-kun...

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.180
<i>Stop crying!</i>

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.710
<i>I'm the one who decided to cast aside</i>

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:04.840
<i>the one person who could wipe away my tears.</i>

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:06.620
<i>I don't deserve to...</i>

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:08.850
Ayai.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:15.860
Just this once, let's go back in time, Ayai.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:23.430
Irido-kun...

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:28.140
Irido-kun... Irido-kun!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:29.690
Ayai...

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:42.840
So, what was it that you 
wanted to talk to me about?

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:48.460
Your first love.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.380
Huh?

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:53.880
When I realized it must be Madoka-san,

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.900
it really bothered me for some reason.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.250
I couldn't sit still.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:01.320
You think Madoka-san was my first love?

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.360
Huh?

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:04.040
Sh-She wasn't?

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:07.390
I don't recall ever having feelings for her.

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.830
B-But yesterday, you said...

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:11.320
Yesterday?

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:15.580
I thought you were acting strange after 
asking me such a weird question.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.740
So <i>that's</i> what got into your head?

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.810
You've got so much going for you on paper,

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:25.460
but you're a real mess under 
the hood, you know that?

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.220
Your nose is running, by the way.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:30.180
Huh?!

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:33.100
Just kidding.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.360
What's so funny?

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.820
Just that you can be such a child, you know?

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:47.070
See? Didn't I tell you?

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:47.910
Huh?

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.500
My first love loved to laugh.
